WHAT THE DATA IS, SO IT IS NOT MISREAD

62 scanning electron micrographs, uint16 TIFF, up to 6144x4376 px, of 316H
stainless steel (as-built, HIP'd, and cast) and MAR superalloy specimens,
imaged with CBS, ETD, SE and BSE detectors.

Two caveats that matter for reuse:

  - The images are stored zlib-compressed inside the TIFF. This is LOSSLESS:
    pixel values are bit-identical to the microscope's originals, verified
    per image. They are not resampled, contrast-adjusted, or cropped.

  - Only 39 of the 62 images carry human correction masks, and those masks
    adjudicate only 1.8-4% of each image's pixels. A mask value of 0 means
    "never reviewed", NOT "not a crack". Treating unreviewed pixels as
    negatives will produce badly optimistic specificity -- this is a real
    hazard and it bit this project's own early measurements. See
    docs/MODEL_VALIDATION_BENCHMARK.md.

The scale bar sits in the SEM databar, which this pipeline crops before
analysis, so no micrometres-per-pixel factor is recoverable from these files.
All measurements in this repository are in pixels.
